{
  "text": " We have openly said that we want to meet with anybody and everybody who will hear us. This is not a left issue, this is not a right issue, this is an American issue. We are by no means leaning to the right or to the left on this topic. This is a people's movement. This is for the people. In our convoy right now, there are Democrats, there are Republicans, there are Independents, there are Libertarians, there are Constitutionalists. There are people that don't affiliate with either party in any way, shape, or form. They just believe in their God-given rights and that's why they're a part of this. We would love the opportunity to speak to the administration personally. We would love the opportunity to speak with any member of the House and any member of the Senate. We would love that opportunity. Come hear the stories of these people. Come down to Haverstown at night and speak to these drivers one-on-one. And by the way, it's not just the truck drivers. The truck drivers stood up. There's no doubt about it. But this is an American people convoy. This is the people's convoy. This convoy consists of RVs, motor homes, cars, motorcycles, shoot a golf cart if you can keep up. Come on down. This is for everybody. This is for the American people. I don't care if you're far left or far right. This is for you too.",
